  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining the Vision**\n\nOkay, I\'m solidifying the vision. My main focus now is **Banquet Pro**, a SaaS application for banquet management. I\'m prioritizing its structure based on the provided mockups. The dashboard overview is my initial target, and I am zeroing in on defining the key metrics to showcase. The \"Banquetely\" branding will subtly weave in where requested.\n\n\n**Outlining Dashboard Components**\n\nI\'m now detailing the core components. I\'m focusing on \"Bookings\" with the master list and a \"New Booking\" drawer. After that, I will be working on a mobile dashboard, ensuring responsiveness. Then, I plan to tackle the \"Calendar View\" and the \"Enquiries Pipeline\" next. I\'m visualizing the data and interactions required for each module.\n\n\n**Expanding Feature Scope**\n\nOkay, I\'m fleshing out the catering catalog, including starters, mains, desserts, and beverages with toggle switches, editing options, and a print feature. The Settings module is also in progress with general profile, venue configuration, pricing rules, and user roles. My current focus is to design this all into a functional, single-page application with a rich React state that encompasses all the functionalities and features seamlessly.\nI\'m also doing a quick check and will be working with local state and `localStorage` to keep things simple.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Prototype Elements**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the front-end requirements. I\'m focusing on creating a client-side prototype with multiple screens, in line with the specified goals. I\'m ensuring everything is a clean SPA. I\'ve also incorporated the images, copying the exact URLs from the HTML. The logo URL is now added, as is Rajesh Kumar\'s profile image.\n\n\n**Incorporating User Profiles**\n\nI\'m now integrating user profiles. I\'m adding Alex Rivera, Alex Rivers (Hospitality executive), and Alex Rivera (Site Admin), along with their associated image URLs. The focus is on linking these profiles to relevant data within the application for proper authorization and personalization.\n\n\n**Adding User Profiles**\n\nI\'m now integrating another user profile. I\'ve added James Wilson, complete with his image URL, into the application. I will focus on proper association within the software to maintain data integrity, allowing for permissions and personalization. I have also added two more profile images as placeholders.\n\n\n**Adding Food Images**\n\nI\'m now integrating food images for the catering catalog. I\'ve added images for Truffle Mushroom Bruschetta, Seared Atlantic Scallops, and Artisan Caesar Salad. Each image URL is now in place for display within the catalog.\n\n\n**Adding More Food Images**\n\nI\'ve integrated more food images into the catering catalog, specifically for Herb-Crusted Rack of Lamb, Miso-Glazed Sea Bass, and Butternut Squash Risotto. Each URL is now correctly incorporated, enhancing the visual appeal of the catalog.\n\n\n**Adding Venue Images**\n\nOkay, I\'m now incorporating venue images. I\'ve added the \"Grand Ballroom,\" \"Emerald Lawns,\" and logo images, complete with their respective URLs. The aim is to enhance visual appeal within the application by integrating these components seamlessly.\n\n\n\n**Structuring the Project**\n\nI\'m now focusing on organizing the project for modularity. I\'m creating `src/types.ts` to define data structures for bookings, enquiries, and other elements. I\'m splitting screens into React components: `Sidebar`, `Header`, `DashboardView`, `BookingsView`, `EnquiriesView`, and `CalendarView`. The application now has a responsive navigation and profile integration.\n\n\n**Implementing the Menu**\n\nI\'m now implementing the catering catalog and settings modules with `MenuView.tsx` and `SettingsView.tsx` respectively, as independent components. I\'ve designed the catalog to include starters, mains, desserts, and beverages with toggle switches and a print menu modal. The settings section will feature tabbed configurations. I have also verified all icons and confirm that I will use Lucide icons exclusively from now on.\n\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the `metadata.json` file to prepare for updating the application name and description to match the \"Banquet Pro\" banquet management SaaS as shown in the requested mockups."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 19
      nanos: 101781025
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
