    thinking: "**Planning UI Components**\n\nOkay, I\'m currently assessing the necessary image assets and libraries for the interface. I\'ve sketched out the key sub-components: a responsive mobile layout with bottom navigation, a desktop sidebar for navigation, and integrated search functionality. I\'m focusing on defining the scope of each sub-component for more efficient implementation.\n\n\n**Defining the Design Palette**\n\nI\'m now establishing the design system\'s aesthetic, which is a modern \"Royal Blue\" theme. The color palette is specified and includes surface, primary, secondary, and accent colors with their hex codes, along with a preference for ambient shadows and soft rounded elements. I\'m prioritizing cohesive, deep, rich styling. Additionally, I\'m thinking about separating the initial data seeding into a file (`/src/data.ts`) to maintain modularity. Finally, I\'m considering initial data, profile image options (Alex Rivera as default for the Lead Admin), and example inquiries.\n\n\n**Compiling Customer Data**\n\nI\'m now collating details on potential and confirmed events. I have a list of new leads, including James K.\'s corporate seminar. I\'ve also integrated the event booking details. I\'m focusing on parsing and structuring the raw input data.\n\n\n**Organizing Event Details**\n\nI\'m now consolidating event data, moving beyond individual bookings to a unified calendar view. The initial entries are integrated, and I\'m adding comprehensive details, including event names, dates, times, locations, and booking statuses. I\'ve compiled several confirmed events and am preparing for a robust bookings list. I am focusing on structuring catering options for completeness.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create a data file `/src/data.ts` populated with initial mock data directly matching the designs and mockups. This allows us to keep our application code clean, modular, and maintainable. This file will export predefined records for bookings, enquiries, catering items, venue settings, spaces, and roles."
