  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Multi-Tenant System**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the multi-tenant system within `App.tsx` and `LoginScreen.tsx`, specifically concerning local storage synchronization. Initially, I\'m thinking that when `App.tsx` boots, I\'ll read the `tenants` data from localStorage. If none is found, it will initialize with a default list, including a pre-configured tenant.\n\n\n**Implementing Tenant State**\n\nI\'ve decided to keep track of the `tenants` state within `App.tsx` and have successfully implemented localStorage synchronization! When the application starts, it reads the `tenants` data from localStorage, or initializes with the `defaultTenants` if no data is found. Updates to the `tenants` state are now automatically serialized and saved to localStorage. Now, I need to figure out how to reference the active tenant in `App.tsx`.\n\n\n**Defining Active Tenant Logic**\n\nI\'ve determined how to find the active tenant using the `activeTenantId` from localStorage. I now fetch it by looking it up in the `tenants` state array. I plan to use separate React state variables for data such as enquiries and bookings for easy updates and syncing to the currently active tenant. Also, I\'ve successfully implemented state synchronization, so when the active tenant\'s data changes, it updates the `tenants` array in state, and persists.\n\n\n**Refining Syncing Logic**\n\nI\'ve just added a new `useEffect` that listens for changes in `activeTenantId`, and, when detected, updates local React state such as enquiries, bookings, venueSpaces, etc. to match the active tenant\'s saved records. The key is to prevent infinite loops by only updating when the active tenant changes, or when the data from any of the local React state changes. I\'m now verifying it is bug-free.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will edit `/src/components/LoginScreen.tsx` to support multi-tenant registration and selection. The login screen will feature:\n1. A **Banquet Hall Selector** dropdown loaded dynamically from the localStorage tenant list.\n2. Two tabs: **Log In to Venue** and **Register New Banquet Hall (Owner)**.\n3. Registration form allowing a new owner to instantly provision their own tenant workspace with unique custom credentials (for both themselves as Owner/Admin and their respective staff/sales agents).\n4. Direct routing so staff logging in with their specific tenant credentials automatically enter that correct tenant context."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 657532575
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
