  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing Implementation Success**\n\nI\'m thrilled! The build was lightning-fast and error-free, succeeding in just 5 seconds. I\'ve been reviewing the recent changes, which included modifications to `/src/types.ts` to enrich the `Booking` interface with `timeSlot` and `startTime` properties, as well as an update to `/src/data`. I\'m now verifying these implementations.\n\n\n**Refining New Booking Features**\n\nI\'ve been improving the new booking flow. I\'ve enriched the initial bookings, now including standard slots and real catering dishes instead of general categories. I\'ve re-written `/src/components/NewBookingDrawer.tsx` to accept the bookings data, render both morning and evening slot options, and allow for a specific start time, defaulted to the selected slot. There\'s now real-time scheduling checks, and responsive conflict warnings. It\'s ready for testing!\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully completed the implementation of the requested booking conflict guards, slot selectors, and dynamic catering item selection features!\n\n### Summary of Improvements\n\nHere is a conceptual and visual overview of the newly added features:\n\n- **Time Slots & Validation (`Double-Booking Protection`)**:\n  - Implemented standard **Morning** and **Evening** time slots when scheduling any event.\n  - Added real-time conflict scanning that alerts you if a booking already exists for the selected date, venue space, and time slot. The system automatically displays a localized alert (supporting English and Hindi) and disables the submission button to prevent double-bookings.\n  - Included a **Start Time Selector** (using native time pickers) that dynamically suggests sensible defaults based on the selected slot (e.g., *10:00 AM* for Morning slots and *6:00 PM* for Evening slots), while remaining fully customizable.\n\n- **Granular Catering Selection (`Dish-by-Dish Menu Allocation`)**:\n  - Replaced the simple category string list with an interactive, categorized checklist. \n  - Catering options are dynamically loaded and organized into **Starters**, **Main Courses**, **Desserts**, and **Beverages**. Users can select the specific dishes that will be served at the event, which are then attached directly to the contract.\n\n- **Polished Presentation Interfaces (`Billing Hub & Calendar Agenda`)**:\n  - **Billing & Invoice Hub**: Now displays the selected slot, start time, and a tag-cloud of the specifically chosen catering dishes for the active booking in the side panel.\n  - **Interactive Calendar**: Shows a clean badge with a clock icon on selected days, highlighting the exact slot and event start time on the day\'s agenda.\n\n- **Full Multi-Tenant Localization**:\n  - Integrated full localization, ensuring all warnings, labels, and forms adapt seamlessly when you switch the system language to Hindi.\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 156800895
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
